  "query_preview": "period of dew points in the 60s-low 70s, given \npersistent southwest flow. This is much more of a typical El \nNino summer pattern than what much of 2026 has brought thus far.\n\nA closer inspection of the overall environment suggests heavy \nrainfall with low chances for organized convection, given high \nPWATs paired with weak shear and mid-level lapse rates. However \ngiven the scattered diurnal nature, it is likely each day will \nfeature stretches of dry, albeit humid conditions too. \nTemperatures will be seasonable in the 80s, but it will \ncertainly feel like midsummer with the increased humidity.",
